{
  "_what_this_is": "Ordered instance sizes per AWS family, GCE machine-type specs, and RDS classes used by design-refs/compute.md and design-refs/database.md to size from measured utilization (skills/gcp-to-aws/scripts/size-from-utilization.py reads this file; nothing is computed from prose). graviton.md maps families; this file lists the sizes inside them.",
  "_like_for_like_anchor": "The smallest size in the mapped AWS family whose vcpu AND memory_gib are both at or above the source's declared vcpu and memory. graviton.md's six explicit rows are special cases of this rule and must agree with it (tests/test_gcp_utilization_sizing.py checks). The step cap in knowledge/estimate/rightsizing-thresholds.json counts positions down from the anchor within the same family list.",
  "_units": "vcpu is the guest-visible vCPU count. memory_gib is GiB (GCE publishes machine memory in GB that are binary GiB). reserved_vcpu is the fraction of a physical core a shared-core type is guaranteed; compute.googleapis.com/instance/cpu/utilization is a fraction of THAT, so it exceeds 1.0 under load and the sizing formula multiplies cpu.p95 by reserved_vcpu when present, else by vcpu.",
